 "recap": [
  "The older alphabet has 20 letters; c, f, j, ñ, q, v, x, z were added later for names and loanwords.",
  "Vowels are short and pure; every syllable is clear.",
  "ng is one sound, ñ is n + y, and r is a quick tap.",
  "Six diphthongs: ay, aw, ey, iw, oy, uy.",
  "Loanwords are respelled by sound: c to k or s, f to p, v to b, qua to kwa, and so on."
 ]
}